# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# <body>
#
# <footer>

# Type should be one of the following:
# * feat (new feature)
# * fix (bug fix)
# * docs (documentation)
# * style (formatting, missing semicolons, etc; no code change)
# * refactor (refactoring production code)
# * test (adding tests, refactoring test; no production code change)
# * chore (updating build tasks, package manager configs, etc; no production code change)
# * perf (performance improvements)
# * ci (continuous integration related)
# * build (build related changes)
# * revert (reverting a previous commit)
#
# Scope is optional and should be the area of the application affected:
# * api (API routes)
# * ui (UI components)
# * store (State management)
# * camera (Camera functionality)
# * ai (AI integration)
# * products (Product management)
# * auth (Authentication)
# * db (Database)
# * config (Configuration)
#
# Subject should use imperative mood and be 50 characters or less
# Body should explain what and why vs. how (optional)
# Footer should reference issues (optional)
#
# Examples:
# feat(camera): add photo capture with quantity selection
# fix(api): resolve OpenAI API timeout issue
# docs: update setup instructions for new developers
# refactor(store): simplify product state management
# test(camera): add unit tests for photo capture component